NAME: Trades wave prep
OWNER: Trades Outreach
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every Tuesday at 7:41 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Trades wave prep" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Trades wave prep · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Tommy only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Trades wave prep · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Trades wave prep · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Trades wave prep · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Trades wave prep · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/ for one of your items (BOT: trades-outreach) that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-trades-outreach.md yet, act on it with the cold-email-wave skill (a wave: Part 2; a reply: Part 3; no: mark the rows back to listed; change: rebuild as a new item). In test mode, never call the cold email tool to create or launch anything: write what you would have created to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-trades-outreach/ and do it first. A "hold outreach" job means: build lists, but prepare no wave until a job lifts it.
Then use the trades-list-build skill for the next trade, unless the trades list already has 25 or more "listed" businesses.
Then use the cold-email-wave skill, Part 1, to prepare one wave from the trades list: pre-flight first, then pick, de-duplicate, verify with treg, write each first line, build the four-touch sequence, run the QC, and put the whole wave in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/trades-outreach/ as one item. Never create or launch a campaign in this routine unless a decision for it is already in approved/decisions/. If the pre-flight fails, the list work still counts: write "wave blocked: <reason>" and carry on to the note. If you already have a wave waiting for Tommy, prepare no second one.
If no decision or job came in, no list work was possible and no wave is waiting to be built, write NO_CHANGE and stop.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/trades-outreach.md: decisions acted on, campaigns created or launched (name, leads, readback result), the trades worked and their counts, the wave waiting for Tommy, businesses "for" another bot, anything blocked and why, and anything needing Tommy. Send nothing to anyone but Tommy's approved recipients.
